# Realtime Voice Rules

## Boundary
The realtime voice system consists of Asterisk, SIP Edge and Pipecat. Django remains the source of truth for providers, billing, agents and call records.

## Preserve contracts
Before modifying telephony/realtime code, inspect existing edge, Asterisk and Pipecat contracts. Do not change wire formats or endpoints casually. Any contract change requires an explicit compatibility/migration plan and integration tests.

## Call lifecycle
Model call lifecycle explicitly: start, answer, terminal state, artifacts, tools, transfers and billing/usage reconciliation. Provider events may arrive late, duplicated or out of order; handlers must be idempotent and state-aware.

## Realtime performance
- Never perform slow database/reporting/integration work synchronously in the audio path unless bounded and required.
- Use short timeouts, bounded retries and safe fallback behavior.
- Capture STT/TTS/LLM/provider latency metrics where available.
- Use backpressure and bounded concurrency.
- Do not rely on process-local tenant state for correctness.

## Agent runtime security
- Enforce tenant/customer/agent authorization before bootstrap/runtime configuration.
- Agent tools/actions are explicit allowlists; never allow arbitrary tool execution.
- Validate action input/output schemas.
- Never place integration credentials in prompts, transcripts, logs or client messages.
- Sanitize tool failures; never expose stack traces/secrets to callers.
- Knowledge retrieval must respect Global/Agency/Customer/Agent scope.
- Platform safety instructions cannot be overridden by lower-level instructions.

## Media
Preserve the existing media contract unless explicitly changed by an approved architecture decision. Account for codec/sample-rate boundaries and interruption behavior in tests.

## Failure behavior
If Django/provider dependencies become unavailable, fail according to the approved call contract and document whether the call should continue, fallback, transfer or terminate. Do not invent a grace period.

## Testing
Every realtime change should include unit tests plus contract/integration tests for bootstrap, media framing, provider events, call completion, transfer and failure paths where applicable.
